{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-30ea5f9b-ce11-4786-82c4-dc6fc69ae85e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b873df04b7d10159","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E001.md","content":"# Investigate RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism for MaaS on xKS\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategic dependency on RHCL (Red Hat Common Libraries) for MaaS authentication and rate limiting on non-OpenShift Kubernetes. It answers three linked questions: (1) is RHCL official xKS support committed by the OpenShift team, (2) are official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts available for xKS (CKS in particular), and (3) can Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) actually be installed and function on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass. The outcome selects one of three bounded deployment mechanisms and gates all downstream deployment, authentication-configuration, and Kuadrant logging work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to confirm official xKS support commitment and timeline (escalate to product leadership if not committed, per the strategy's Sprint 1 directive).\n- Determine whether official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts exist or are planned for xKS, and their maturity.\n- Validate Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) installation on a CKS test environment with the Istio GatewayClass, confirming the Gateway API implementation confirmed available on CoreWeave.\n- Produce a decision record selecting the deployment mechanism, with evidence:\n  - Outcome A: official RHCL Helm charts (primary).\n  - Outcome B: standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm (fallback).\n  - Outcome C: direct Envoy ext_authz integration without Kuadrant (contingency).\n- Document known constraints of the selected mechanism for the downstream deployment and validation work.\n\nOut of scope: implementing the selected deployment (that is the conditional downstream work this investigation gates), and MaaS application changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written decision exists stating which deployment mechanism (RHCL official Helm charts, standalone Authorino + Limitador, or direct Envoy ext_authz) will be used for MaaS on xKS, with the evidence behind it.\n- The RHCL/OpenShift team's official xKS support position (committed / not committed, with timeline) is documented; if not committed, the escalation to product leadership has been raised and recorded.\n- Kuadrant installation on CKS with Istio GatewayClass has been exercised and the result (works / breaks, and why) is documented, or — if the contingency is selected — the reason Kuadrant is not viable is documented.\n- The decision identifies which downstream conditional plan applies (branch A, B, or C).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input embedded in the strategy).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71418,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"50dc2a54-9acf-479a-8921-24ce8b96e627","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:33:27.913Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
