{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-30ea5f9b-ce11-4786-82c4-dc6fc69ae85e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b452e51f64e76663","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E002.md","content":"# Investigate OIDC group claim configurability in the MaaS Tenant CRD\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the OIDC group claim path can be made configurable in MaaS without breaking MaaS 3.4 GA constraints. The MaaSSubscription controller maps rate-limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`; on xKS, groups must be sourced from the OIDC token's group claim, whose name varies by identity provider (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims). The strategy's primary approach adds a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD, passed through to CEL predicate generation; the fallback (if the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA) documents the required claim format and pushes IdP configuration burden to customers.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine whether the Tenant CRD can be extended post-3.4-GA (is the CRD/API surface frozen; what does the MaaS release/compatibility policy allow on the GA branch).\n- Determine the concrete change surface for a `groupClaimPath` field: Tenant CRD schema, pass-through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (maas-controller), and Helm chart exposure.\n- Produce a decision record with one of two bounded outcomes:\n  - Outcome A: CRD extensible — implement configurable `groupClaimPath` (default `auth.identity.groups`).\n  - Outcome B: CRD frozen — document the required claim format and push IdP configuration burden to customers.\n\nOut of scope: implementing either outcome (that is the conditional downstream work this investigation gates).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written decision exists stating whether the `groupClaimPath` approach (outcome A) or the documented-claim-format fallback (outcome B) applies, citing the MaaS 3.4 GA CRD freeze/compatibility policy evidence.\n- If outcome A: the exact change surface (CRD field, controller pass-through, chart value) is specified so implementation can start without further design work.\n- If outcome B: the required OIDC group claim format and customer IdP configuration responsibilities are identified.\n- The decision identifies which downstream conditional plan applies (branch A or B).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71418,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"66a796a5-2368-4477-b5e0-c5472d3530d6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:33:35.409Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
