C issuer settings, TLS certificate source, and PostgreSQL connection are all configurable via chart values, measured by rendering with non-default values producing the corresponding resources.\n- No OLM or OpenShift-specific resource types are required by the chart, measured by a dry-run render against plain Kubernetes CRDs.\n- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager (not OpenShift service-CA), measured by successful certificate provisioning on a cluster with cert-manager installed.\n- The chart is structured for integration into the RHAII xKS Helm-based installation path (reviewed with the xKS Platform team).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (packaging enabler).\n- HLR-2 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (packaging enabler).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72824,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"df0a7d20-4721-4d5b-8836-9e733c2ce8d9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:33:55.514Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
