{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-57c7df14-5b08-4a57-9f4a-251436d18511","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eacbdc8c70fc2ae","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E005.md","content":"# Add Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api\n\n## Description\n\nInstrument maas-api with Prometheus metrics covering the observability surface the strategy makes a core value proposition (per the Staff Engineer Input embedded in the strategy): token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle (creation, validation, revocation), and inference request latency. maas-api already exposes a dedicated Prometheus metrics listener (port 9090, `internal/metrics` server; prometheus client_golang is an existing dependency), so this extends an existing foundation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add Prometheus counters/gauges for:\n  - API key lifecycle: creation, validation, revocation (`maas_api_key_created_total` and related).\n  - Token usage per user/subscription and inference requests (`maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`).\n  - Rate limiting enforcement (`maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`).\n  - Inference request latency.\n- Expose all metrics on the existing `/metrics` listener, scrape-compatible with the CKS Prometheus instance.\n- Apply the strategy's performance mitigation: asynchronous metric emission; if p99 overhead exceeds 5ms, move emission to post-response goroutines.\n- Verify feasibility against MaaS 3.4 GA code freeze constraints: if maas-api is frozen, deliver the instrumentation as a post-3.4 patch (per the strategy assumption) rather than dropping scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a running maas-api with a user creating an API key, making inference requests, and exceeding a rate limit, then the `/metrics` endpoint exposes `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by scraping the metrics endpoint.\n- Inference request latency metrics are exposed, measured by scraping the metrics endpoint after inference traffic.\n- Metric emission does not degrade request latency beyond the strategy's threshold (p99 overhead ≤ 5ms, or moved to post-response goroutines), measured by load-test comparison before/after instrumentation.\n- Instrumentation is confirmed compatible with the MaaS 3.4 GA branch, or delivered as an identified post-3.4 patch, measured by the build/merge outcome on the target branch.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 [P0]: Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74317,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"2f543b5f-bb1e-406d-a36b-33a815cf406f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:34:06.711Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
