{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-57c7df14-5b08-4a57-9f4a-251436d18511","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb5b30b7d4041458","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E006.md","content":"# Add structured logging to maas-api for xKS observability\n\n## Description\n\nAdd structured (JSON) logging to maas-api covering authentication-related events (API key validation outcomes) and subscription selection decisions, formatted for aggregation in the CKS Grafana Loki infrastructure. This is the maas-api portion of the strategy's P1 logging requirement; Kuadrant-side (Authorino/Limitador) log configuration is separately owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Emit structured JSON log entries for:\n  - API key validation events (success/failure, with reason).\n  - Subscription selection decisions (which tier/subscription was selected for a request).\n- Include the fields the strategy's acceptance criteria require: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason if denied.\n- Format logs with labels/structure suitable for CKS Grafana Loki label-filter queries.\n- Reuse the existing zap structured logging already present in the maas-api codebase.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n- Given a request that triggers subscription selection, when the selection is made, then the decision is logged with the selected subscription/tier, measured by querying Grafana Loki.\n- Log entries are valid structured JSON parseable by the Loki aggregatio