{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c5174b7a-82cd-4316-90be-dc6a8d136fa5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6ad8c4e37ea9d62","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E008.md","content":"# Deploy and validate MaaS on CKS and AKS\n\n## Description\n\nDeploy the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase via the Helm charts on CKS (priority platform per the Staff Engineer Input embedded in the strategy) and then on AKS, validating core MaaS functionality — subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, external OIDC authentication, and API key access — and documenting what works, what breaks, the engineering delta, and all known limitations versus RHOAI MaaS GA. This epic is the Dev Preview deliverable: a functional demonstration, not a production-ready deployment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Deploy MaaS on a CKS cluster (Istio GatewayClass, RHCL/Kuadrant per the selected deployment mechanism) using the Helm chart with OIDC configuration; confirm maas-api and maas-controller pods running and healthy.\n- Deploy MaaS on an AKS cluster and confirm the same healthy-deployment criteria (RFE acceptance criterion: \"AKS AND CKS\").\n- Validate core functionality on both platforms:\n  - Subscription/tier management (CRUD).\n  - Token rate limiting (HTTP 429 on exceeded limits).\n  - External OIDC authentication and API key authentication end-to-end (API key persisted in PostgreSQL and usable for inference).\n- Exercise the strategy's failure modes: Limitador pod termination (HTTP 503), PostgreSQL unavailability (API key creation fails, OIDC auth continues), cert-manager TLS rotation without connection errors.\n- Document known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, and the engineering delta discovered.\n- Manage the MaaS 3.4 build-timing risk: validate against RC builds in parallel while awaiting the stable build; maintain the RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo option.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a CKS cluster with the auth/rate-limiting layer and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n- Given an AKS cluster with the same prerequisites, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated API key.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n- Given a deployment with Limitador terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then it is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and Envoy logs.\n- Given cert-manager-issued TLS certificates are rotated, then active requests continue and new requests succeed, measured by zero connection errors during rotation and successful TLS handshake post-rotation.\n- Given PostgreSQL becomes unavailable, then API key creation fails with HTTP 503 while OIDC token-based authentication continues to succeed, measured by response status and error logs.\n- A document exists listing all known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, including the engineering delta (code changes, configuration changes, Helm chart packaging).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on AKS.\n- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (functional validation).\n- HLR-4 [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated (end-to-end validation).\n- HLR-5 [P0]: API key authentication functional on xKS (end-to-end validation).\n- HLR-9 [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (functional validation).\n- HLR-11 [P1]: Known limitations documented (falls out of this validation work).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75567,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"671c30b7-0479-4f64-b909-11e05415d656","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:34:34.564Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
