, failure modes), measured by technical review against the deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n- The document states what users must do (provide an OIDC-compatible identity provider) and the supported/required claim formats.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-12 [P2]: User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n- Strategy acceptance criteria (User Management): user authentication strategy defined and documented; user identity flow documented.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78276,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c8604ba3bb4d35d","agent_id":"a228e1c2340ee276c","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"3128ab7c-9f05-4825-a811-ef26a8aa4ab2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:35:00.937Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
