{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fcfb6e38-53c0-48f9-8826-3f1a464ab871","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d86ff00ded48ee","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-03pyhi41/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E013.md","content":"# Implement configurable groupClaimPath in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller\n\n## Description\n\nConditional plan (outcome A of the group-claim configurability investigation): the Tenant CRD is extensible post-3.4-GA, so a configurable `groupClaimPath` field is added (default `auth.identity.groups`) and passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation. This lets deployments map OIDC group claims with differing formats (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) to subscription tiers without code changes per identity provider.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add the `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD schema (default: `auth.identity.groups`).\n- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (maas-controller/pkg/controller/maas/maassubscription_controller.go), so tier-mapping predicates read groups from the configured OIDC claim path.\n- Expose `groupClaimPath` as a Helm chart value so the deployment configuration drives it per deployment.\n- Keep the change additive/configuration-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior with the default value is unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n- Given a deployment using the default claim path, when group-based tier 