{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82f63f2cb7d64c9f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E011\n3\ttitle: Document the user identity flow for MaaS on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n16\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n17\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n18\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n19\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n20\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E010\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: -1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\tgated_by: null\n37\tgate_failure_impact: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Document the user identity flow for MaaS on xKS\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tAuthor the user-management documentation for MaaS on xKS: the defined authentication strategy (external OIDC replacing OpenShift identity mapping), the end-to-end user identity flow for xKS deployments, and how external identities map to MaaS subscriptions and tiers. This documentation describes what was actually built, so it runs last and is technically reviewed against the implementation.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Content outline:\n48\t  - User management strategy for xKS: why external OIDC replaces Kubernetes RBAC identity mapping, and what customers must provide (OIDC-compatible identity provider).\n49\t  - User identity flow: customer IdP → OIDC JWT → gateway/Authorino validation → identity injection → subscription/tier selection → API key issuance and use.\n50\t  - Identity-to-subscription mapping: how OIDC group claims map to tiers, including the group claim format supported by the delivered configuration (configurable claim path or documented required format, per the resolved approach).\n51\t  - Known limitations of the Dev Preview versus RHOAI MaaS GA, cross-referenced with the limitations identified during deployment validation.\n52\t  - Failure modes from the user's perspective (IdP outage behavior, API-key vs OIDC dependence).\n53\t- Publish through the Red Hat docs content process.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A published document exists describing the user authentication strategy and the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering the outline above.\n58\t- The documented flow matches the implemented behavior (group claim mapping, OIDC and API key paths, failure modes), measured by technical review against the deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n59\t- The document states what users must do (provide an OIDC-compatible identity provider) and the supported/required claim formats.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-12 [P2]: User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n64\t- Strategy acceptance criteria (User Management): user authentication strategy defined and documented; user identity flow documented.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95cb5a3d3102814f","agent_id":"aaae7d2c38a5bd6a6","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"02d885c6-6a8e-412a-89a5-b343f31c5d90","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:40:24.881Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82f63f2cb7d64c9f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
