{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-966557f37575abf6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E013\n3\ttitle: Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD is later opened for extension, replace this\n16\t    documentation-only fallback with the configurable groupClaimPath implementation.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS on xKS\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tConditional plan (outcome B of the group-claim configurability investigation): the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA, so configurable claim-path mapping cannot be shipped. Instead, the required OIDC group claim format is documented and identity-provider configuration burden is pushed to customers: customers must configure their IdP (or token transformation) to emit groups in the claim format MaaS expects (`auth.identity.groups`).\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS tier/subscription mapping on xKS, including concrete IdP configuration guidance for common providers (e.g., Entra ID, Cognito, Keycloak) to emit or map groups into the required claim.\n42\t- Document this as a known limitation of the xKS Dev Preview versus configurable claim-path mapping.\n43\t- Verify the documented guidance against at least one real identity provider configuration on the CKS validation deployment, so tier mapping works end-to-end with a correctly configured IdP.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A document exists specifying the required OIDC group claim format and per-provider configuration steps, measured by publication and review.\n48\t- Given an OIDC deployment whose IdP is configured per the document, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the user is mapped to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n49\t- The limitation (no configurable claim path in the Dev Preview) is recorded in the known-limitations document, measured by its inclusion.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (fallback: documented required claim format; per-strategy fallback if the Tenant CRD is frozen).\n54\t- HLR-9 [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (via documented claim format).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95cb5a3d3102814f","agent_id":"aaae7d2c38a5bd6a6","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"078ff902-5fc9-4b08-97a0-bcdfb3d395a6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:40:35.859Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-966557f37575abf6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
