 issuance and use.\n50\t  - Identity-to-subscription mapping: how OIDC group claims map to tiers, including the group claim format supported by the delivered configuration (configurable claim path or documented required format, per the resolved approach).\n51\t  - Known limitations of the Dev Preview versus RHOAI MaaS GA, cross-referenced with the limitations identified during deployment validation.\n52\t  - Failure modes from the user's perspective (IdP outage behavior, API-key vs OIDC dependence).\n53\t- Publish through the Red Hat docs content process.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A published document exists describing the user authentication strategy and the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering the outline above.\n58\t- The documented flow matches the implemented behavior (group claim mapping, OIDC and API key paths, failure modes), measured by technical review against the deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n59\t- The document states what users must do (provide an OIDC-compatible identity provider) and the supported/required claim formats.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-12 [P2]: User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n64\t- Strategy acceptance criteria (User Management): user authentication strategy defined and documented; user identity flow documented.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b5e1a98d78bdc7","agent_id":"a724c079c1f66f2f0","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"de0fa5ee-7243-461e-bfe9-46c2c32cab70","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:48:38.166Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-910acc769b03aaab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
