{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be1b3158f31325fa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If RHCL official xKS support or charts are not actually available,\n16\t    fall back to standalone Authorino + Limitador deployment via Helm.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 0\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Low\n30\tai_implementability_score: -1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tConditional plan (outcome A of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment-mechanism investigation): RHCL official xKS support is committed and official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts are used to deploy Authorino and Limitador for MaaS authentication and rate limiting on xKS, starting with CKS. This is the primary deployment path in the strategy's priority order and the long-term supportable option.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Consume the official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts to deploy Authorino and Limitador on CKS (and subsequently AKS) alongside the MaaS Helm chart.\n42\t- Validate the deployed Kuadrant stack supports the MaaS requirements: Authorino OIDC identity source and API key callback authentication, TokenRateLimitPolicy-based rate limiting via Limitador, Gateway API (Istio) integration.\n43\t- Confirm the support commitment's terms (lifecycle, upgrade path) are documented for the Dev Preview.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Authorino and Limitador are deployed on CKS via the official RHCL Helm charts and are healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n48\t- Given a MaaS deployment using this Kuadrant stack, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n49\t- Given the same stack, when a user authenticates via OIDC JWT or `sk-oai-*` API key, then authentication is enforced by Authorino as configured, measured by successful authenticated requests and rejected invalid credentials.\n50\t- The RHCL xKS support terms covering this deployment are documented, measured by a written statement from the RHCL/OpenShift team.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador via official RHCL charts).\n55\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (official-chart path).\n56\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (auth/rate-limiting layer).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b5e1a98d78bdc7","agent_id":"a724c079c1f66f2f0","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"f131ce89-750c-4d5d-8225-00dd41c54996","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:48:42.917Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be1b3158f31325fa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
