Kuadrant components without official RHCL xKS support (Dev Preview risk acceptance), consistent with the product-leadership escalation raised in the investigation.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Standalone Authorino and Limitador are deployed on CKS via Helm and are healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n48\t- Given a MaaS deployment using this stack, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n49\t- Given the same stack, when a user authenticates via OIDC JWT or `sk-oai-*` API key, then authentication is enforced by Authorino as configured, measured by successful authenticated requests and rejected invalid credentials.\n50\t- The support posture and risks of the standalone path are documented and acknowledged, measured by a recorded risk-acceptance note.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (standalone Limitador).\n55\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (fallback path selected and validated).\n56\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (auth/rate-limiting layer).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b5e1a98d78bdc7","agent_id":"a724c079c1f66f2f0","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"c7e60acb-959a-4607-995d-944d00b94c9c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:48:43.835Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9c7d672f13ad123","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
