{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b810d629bfc138","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E010\n3\ttitle: Add distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Add distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tImplement distributed tracing across the MaaS request path on xKS — gateway ingress through Authorino, Limitador, payload-processing, to the model backend — using OpenTelemetry. This is the strategy's P2 observability tier. maas-api already integrates the OpenTelemetry SDK and exports traces via OTLP/gRPC to a collector (architecture context: maas-api/internal/tracing/provider.go), so the work extends an existing foundation to cover the full request path.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Propagate trace context through the full request path: gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing (BBR ext_proc) → model backend.\n39\t- Emit spans for the MaaS-handled segments (maas-api request handling, payload-processing request transformations) via the existing OTel/OTLP export path.\n40\t- Configure trace collection compatible with the xKS observability infrastructure.\n41\t- Validate end-to-end trace continuity on a deployed MaaS instance on CKS.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with tracing enabled, when an inference request is made, then a distributed trace exists covering gateway ingress, Authorino authentication, Limitador rate limiting, payload-processing, and the model backend, measured by retrieving a complete trace (single trace ID across all segments) from the tracing backend.\n46\t- Tracing instrumentation does not observably degrade request latency, measured by load-test comparison before/after.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-13 [P2]: Distributed tracing functional: gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend (per Staff Engineer Input).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b5e1a98d78bdc7","agent_id":"a724c079c1f66f2f0","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"e6821ebe-1ed1-4b98-a624-0b51fe87345f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:48:45.481Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89b810d629bfc138","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
