{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6e3b20fd2cae81","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n3\ttitle: Deploy Perses dashboards and integrate MaaS metrics with CKS Prometheus\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Monitoring\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Deploy Perses dashboards and integrate MaaS metrics with CKS Prometheus\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tDeliver the xKS Platform side of MaaS observability: Perses dashboards visualizing MaaS metrics and integration of the MaaS metrics endpoints with the CKS Prometheus instance. This makes the metrics instrumented in maas-api visible and queryable, which is the \"functional\" bar for the strategy's P0 observability metrics requirement.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Deploy Perses dashboards for MaaS displaying: token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours.\n40\t- Configure the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape the maas-api `/metrics` endpoint (port 9090 listener), validating the assumption that CKS Prometheus scrape targets are accessible for MaaS (strategy assumption marked \"needs validation\" — Sprint 1 confirmation with xKS Platform / CoreWeave).\n41\t- Wire dashboard queries to the metric names and labels emitted by the maas-api instrumentation (`maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`).\n42\t- Validate live-data dashboard rendering and the active maas-api scrape target against the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS — the live-data and scrape-target acceptance criteria can only be exercised on a deployed MaaS instance, which orders this epic after the CKS/AKS deployment validation work.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then the metrics are present in the CKS Prometheus instance, measured by querying Prometheus for the three metric families.\n47\t- Given the Perses dashboards installed, when an admin navigates to the MaaS observability dashboard, then it displays token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours, measured by dashboard rendering with live data.\n48\t- CKS Prometheus scrape-target accessibility for MaaS endpoints is confirmed and documented (or the gap escalated to the xKS Platform / CoreWeave owners), measured by an active scrape target for maas-api.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-8 [P0]: Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (integration/visibility portion).\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951f52331839b74d","agent_id":"a2f970ffe7fafef2b","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"51a168a7-8ecc-4e85-b8c3-d4b61dbc997a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:57:23.578Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6e3b20fd2cae81","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
