{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-805085ef68ab6458","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-C-E012\n3\ttitle: Integrate direct Envoy ext_authz authentication and rate limiting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If direct Envoy ext_authz cannot enforce the required auth and\n17\t    rate-limit semantics, the Dev Preview scope must be renegotiated with product\n18\t    leadership (no further fallback defined in the strategy).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 0\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Integrate direct Envoy ext_authz authentication and rate limiting\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional plan (outcome C of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment-mechanism investigation — contingency): Kuadrant is not viable on xKS, so authentication and rate limiting are integrated directly at Envoy via the ext_authz filter, bypassing Authorino/Limitador. This is the strategy's contingency path; if it is selected, the Authorino-based OIDC configuration approach is rewritten to target Envoy ext_authz instead. This epic also owns the mechanism-dependent end-to-end validation — authentication enforcement and token rate limiting exercised against a deployed, OIDC-configured MaaS instance — because that validation hinges on this deployment path's work product.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Configure Envoy ext_authz to enforce MaaS authentication: external OIDC JWT validation and API key callback validation against maas-api's `/internal/v1/api-keys/validate` endpoint.\n44\t- Implement token rate limiting at the gateway layer equivalent to the MaaSSubscription tier limits previously enforced via TokenRateLimitPolicy/Limitador.\n45\t- Integrate with the Istio data plane on CKS (EnvoyFilter-level configuration where needed).\n46\t- Validate the ext_authz enforcement path end-to-end against the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS, including the enforcement-unavailability failure mode (requests denied while the ext_authz path is unavailable).\n47\t- Document the capability deltas versus the Kuadrant-based paths (features lost, behavioral differences) for the known-limitations record.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a MaaS deployment on CKS using direct Envoy ext_authz, when a user presents a valid OIDC JWT or `sk-oai-*` API key, then the request is authenticated, measured by successful authenticated requests and rejected invalid credentials.\n52\t- Given a user exceeding a configured token rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n53\t- Given the Envoy ext_authz enforcement path unavailable, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503 (fail-closed), measured by response status and Envoy logs.\n54\t- Capability deltas versus the Kuadrant-based deployment are documented, measured by inclusion in the known-limitations document.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (gateway-layer enforcement, end-to-end validation).\n59\t- HLR-4 [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated (via Envoy ext_authz in this contingency).\n60\t- HLR-5 [P0]: API key authentication functional on xKS (end-to-end via the ext_authz callback path).\n61\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (contingency path selected and validated).\n62\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (auth/rate-limiting layer).\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951f52331839b74d","agent_id":"a2f970ffe7fafef2b","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"f7424806-9af2-4bfc-bbcc-85187e8492ba","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:57:34.391Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-805085ef68ab6458","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
