{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0af42364f023bd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E013\n3\ttitle: Implement configurable groupClaimPath in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD turns out to be frozen after deeper analysis,\n16\t    switch to documenting the required OIDC group claim format and pushing IdP configuration\n17\t    burden to customers.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Implement configurable groupClaimPath in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional plan (outcome A of the group-claim configurability investigation): the Tenant CRD is extensible post-3.4-GA, so a configurable `groupClaimPath` field is added (default `auth.identity.groups`) and passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation. This lets deployments map OIDC group claims with differing formats (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) to subscription tiers without code changes per identity provider.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add the `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD schema (default: `auth.identity.groups`).\n43\t- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (maas-controller/pkg/controller/maas/maassubscription_controller.go), so tier-mapping predicates read groups from the configured OIDC claim path.\n44\t- Expose `groupClaimPath` as a Helm chart value so the deployment configuration drives it per deployment.\n45\t- Keep the change additive/configuration-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior with the default value is unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n50\t- Given a deployment using the default claim path, when group-based tier mapping is exercised, then behavior is identical to the current (RHOAI) implementation, measured by existing tier-mapping tests passing unchanged.\n51\t- The field is configurable per deployment via the Helm chart, measured by rendering with a non-default claim path producing the corresponding Tenant configuration.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n56\t- HLR-9 [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ace5ef834c7ebcc","agent_id":"aaf3692cfeb50acdd","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"8cfd6909-ffbd-48d9-9736-b74fdc91441a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:07:16.108Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0af42364f023bd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
