5\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with tracing enabled, when an inference request is made, then a distributed trace exists covering gateway ingress, Authorino authentication, Limitador rate limiting, payload-processing, and the model backend, measured by retrieving a complete trace (single trace ID across all segments) from the tracing backend.\n46\t- Tracing instrumentation does not observably degrade request latency, measured by load-test comparison before/after.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-13 [P2]: Distributed tracing functional: gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend (per Staff Engineer Input).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ace5ef834c7ebcc","agent_id":"aaf3692cfeb50acdd","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"6e21922e-ba5f-442a-9ff2-96c73b301814","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:07:17.770Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86635b845f11cf13","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
