{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a95759f60ae1a050","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If RHCL official xKS support or charts are not actually available,\n17\t    fall back to standalone Authorino + Limitador deployment via Helm.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Deploy Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional plan (outcome A of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment-mechanism investigation): RHCL official xKS support is committed and official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts are used to deploy Authorino and Limitador for MaaS authentication and rate limiting on xKS, starting with CKS. This is the primary deployment path in the strategy's priority order and the long-term supportable option. This epic also owns the mechanism-dependent end-to-end validation — authentication enforcement and token rate limiting exercised against a deployed, OIDC-configured MaaS instance — because that validation hinges on this deployment path's work product.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Consume the official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts to deploy Authorino and Limitador on CKS (and subsequently AKS) alongside the MaaS Helm chart.\n43\t- Validate the deployed Kuadrant stack end-to-end against the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS: Authorino OIDC identity source and API key callback authentication, TokenRateLimitPolicy-based rate limiting via Limitador (HTTP 429 on exceeded token limits), and Gateway API (Istio) integration.\n44\t- Exercise the enforcement-layer failure mode: with the Limitador pod terminated, inference requests are denied with HTTP 503.\n45\t- Confirm the support commitment's terms (lifecycle, upgrade path) are documented for the Dev Preview.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Authorino and Limitador are deployed on CKS via the official RHCL Helm charts and are healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n50\t- Given a MaaS deployment using this Kuadrant stack, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n51\t- Given the same stack, when a user authenticates via OIDC JWT or `sk-oai-*` API key, then authentication is enforced by Authorino as configured, measured by successful authenticated requests and rejected invalid credentials.\n52\t- Given the deployed stack with the Limitador pod terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n53\t- The RHCL xKS support terms covering this deployment are documented, measured by a written statement from the RHCL/OpenShift team.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador via official RHCL charts, end-to-end validation).\n58\t- HLR-4 [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated (end-to-end via Authorino on the official-chart path).\n59\t- HLR-5 [P0]: API key authentication functional on xKS (end-to-end via the Authorino callback path).\n60\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (official-chart path).\n61\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (auth/rate-limiting layer).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ace5ef834c7ebcc","agent_id":"aaf3692cfeb50acdd","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"bac1c634-4392-43d5-80ab-270827d249f5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:07:23.331Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a95759f60ae1a050","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
