{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc19cc73864adddf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E012\n3\ttitle: Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador on xKS via Helm\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If standalone Kuadrant components cannot be installed on the\n17\t    target platform, escalate to the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 7\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador on xKS via Helm\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional plan (outcome B of the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment-mechanism investigation): RHCL official xKS support is not committed, so Authorino and Limitador are deployed standalone via Helm (without the RHCL distribution layer) to provide MaaS authentication and rate limiting on xKS, starting with CKS. This is the strategy's fallback deployment path. This epic also owns the mechanism-dependent end-to-end validation — authentication enforcement and token rate limiting exercised against a deployed, OIDC-configured MaaS instance — because that validation hinges on this deployment path's work product.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Deploy standalone Authorino and Limitador via their Helm charts on CKS (and subsequently AKS), configured for the MaaS gateway (Istio GatewayClass) integration.\n43\t- Validate the standalone stack end-to-end against the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS: Authorino OIDC identity source and API key callback authentication, TokenRateLimitPolicy-based rate limiting via Limitador (HTTP 429 on exceeded token limits).\n44\t- Exercise the enforcement-layer failure mode: with the Limitador pod terminated, inference requests are denied with HTTP 503.\n45\t- Document the support implications of running Kuadrant components without official RHCL xKS support (Dev Preview risk acceptance), consistent with the product-leadership escalation raised in the investigation.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Standalone Authorino and Limitador are deployed on CKS via Helm and are healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n50\t- Given a MaaS deployment using this stack, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n51\t- Given the same stack, when a user authenticates via OIDC JWT or `sk-oai-*` API key, then authentication is enforced by Authorino as configured, measured by successful authenticated requests and rejected invalid credentials.\n52\t- Given the deployed stack with the Limitador pod terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n53\t- The support posture and risks of the standalone path are documented and acknowledged, measured by a recorded risk-acceptance note.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (standalone Limitador, end-to-end validation).\n58\t- HLR-4 [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated (end-to-end via Authorino on the standalone path).\n59\t- HLR-5 [P0]: API key authentication functional on xKS (end-to-end via the Authorino callback path).\n60\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (fallback path selected and validated).\n61\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (auth/rate-limiting layer).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ace5ef834c7ebcc","agent_id":"aaf3692cfeb50acdd","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"229949b4-a47c-4c46-b4c5-a4eb2d91c6c7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:07:39.315Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc19cc73864adddf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
