{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8346a73b58d988b8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism for MaaS on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate RHCL/Kuadrant deployment mechanism for MaaS on xKS\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategic dependency on RHCL (Red Hat Common Libraries) for MaaS authentication and rate limiting on non-OpenShift Kubernetes. It answers three linked questions: (1) is RHCL official xKS support committed by the OpenShift team, (2) are official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts available for xKS (CKS in particular), and (3) can Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) actually be installed and function on a CKS cluster with the Istio GatewayClass. The outcome selects one of three bounded deployment mechanisms and gates all downstream deployment, authentication-configuration, and Kuadrant logging work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to confirm official xKS support commitment and timeline (escalate to product leadership if not committed, per the strategy's Sprint 1 directive).\n34\t- Determine whether official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts exist or are planned for xKS, and their maturity.\n35\t- Validate Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) installation on a CKS test environment with the Istio GatewayClass, confirming the Gateway API implementation confirmed available on CoreWeave.\n36\t- Produce a decision record selecting the deployment mechanism, with evidence:\n37\t  - Outcome A: official RHCL Helm charts (primary).\n38\t  - Outcome B: standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm (fallback).\n39\t  - Outcome C: direct Envoy ext_authz integration without Kuadrant (contingency).\n40\t- Document known constraints of the selected mechanism for the downstream deployment and validation work.\n41\t\n42\tOut of scope: implementing the selected deployment (that is the conditional downstream work this investigation gates), and MaaS application changes.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- A written decision exists stating which deployment mechanism (RHCL official Helm charts, standalone Authorino + Limitador, or direct Envoy ext_authz) will be used for MaaS on xKS, with the evidence behind it.\n47\t- The RHCL/OpenShift team's official xKS support position (committed / not committed, with timeline) is documented; if not committed, the escalation to product leadership has been raised and recorded.\n48\t- Kuadrant installation on CKS with Istio GatewayClass has been exercised and the result (works / breaks, and why) is documented, or — if the contingency is selected — the reason Kuadrant is not viable is documented.\n49\t- The decision identifies which downstream conditional plan applies (branch A, B, or C).\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-7 [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input embedded in the strategy).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"1dfe73e5-477d-4dfe-8c29-ce96d67fa767","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:28.212Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8346a73b58d988b8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
