{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5617b4dc20f01cc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate OIDC group claim configurability in the MaaS Tenant CRD\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate OIDC group claim configurability in the MaaS Tenant CRD\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the OIDC group claim path can be made configurable in MaaS without breaking MaaS 3.4 GA constraints. The MaaSSubscription controller maps rate-limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`; on xKS, groups must be sourced from the OIDC token's group claim, whose name varies by identity provider (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims). The strategy's primary approach adds a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD, passed through to CEL predicate generation; the fallback (if the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA) documents the required claim format and pushes IdP configuration burden to customers.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Determine whether the Tenant CRD can be extended post-3.4-GA (is the CRD/API surface frozen; what does the MaaS release/compatibility policy allow on the GA branch).\n34\t- Determine the concrete change surface for a `groupClaimPath` field: Tenant CRD schema, pass-through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (maas-controller), and Helm chart exposure.\n35\t- Produce a decision record with one of two bounded outcomes:\n36\t  - Outcome A: CRD extensible — implement configurable `groupClaimPath` (default `auth.identity.groups`).\n37\t  - Outcome B: CRD frozen — document the required claim format and push IdP configuration burden to customers.\n38\t\n39\tOut of scope: implementing either outcome (that is the conditional downstream work this investigation gates).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A written decision exists stating whether the `groupClaimPath` approach (outcome A) or the documented-claim-format fallback (outcome B) applies, citing the MaaS 3.4 GA CRD freeze/compatibility policy evidence.\n44\t- If outcome A: the exact change surface (CRD field, controller pass-through, chart value) is specified so implementation can start without further design work.\n45\t- If outcome B: the required OIDC group claim format and customer IdP configuration responsibilities are identified.\n46\t- The decision identifies which downstream conditional plan applies (branch A or B).\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"883c164b-e18f-42b1-ac14-a44bd96bc323","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:29.053Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5617b4dc20f01cc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
