{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-805026a149a97090","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n3\ttitle: Add Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Add Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tInstrument maas-api with Prometheus metrics covering the observability surface the strategy makes a core value proposition (per the Staff Engineer Input embedded in the strategy): token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle (creation, validation, revocation), and inference request latency. maas-api already exposes a dedicated Prometheus metrics listener (port 9090, `internal/metrics` server; prometheus client_golang is an existing dependency), so this extends an existing foundation.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Add Prometheus counters/gauges for:\n38\t  - API key lifecycle: creation, validation, revocation (`maas_api_key_created_total` and related).\n39\t  - Token usage per user/subscription and inference requests (`maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`).\n40\t  - Rate limiting enforcement (`maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`).\n41\t  - Inference request latency.\n42\t- Expose all metrics on the existing `/metrics` listener, scrape-compatible with the CKS Prometheus instance.\n43\t- Apply the strategy's performance mitigation: asynchronous metric emission; if p99 overhead exceeds 5ms, move emission to post-response goroutines.\n44\t- Verify feasibility against MaaS 3.4 GA code freeze constraints: if maas-api is frozen, deliver the instrumentation as a post-3.4 patch (per the strategy assumption) rather than dropping scope.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given a running maas-api with a user creating an API key, making inference requests, and exceeding a rate limit, then the `/metrics` endpoint exposes `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by scraping the metrics endpoint.\n49\t- Inference request latency metrics are exposed, measured by scraping the metrics endpoint after inference traffic.\n50\t- Metric emission does not degrade request latency beyond the strategy's threshold (p99 overhead ≤ 5ms, or moved to post-response goroutines), measured by load-test comparison before/after instrumentation.\n51\t- Instrumentation is confirmed compatible with the MaaS 3.4 GA branch, or delivered as an identified post-3.4 patch, measured by the build/merge outcome on the target branch.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-8 [P0]: Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input).\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"b84996eb-a315-4153-8d2e-f3a31f70c900","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:34.256Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-805026a149a97090","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
