{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a499e8c9bc08d29a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n3\ttitle: Configure structured logging for Kuadrant auth and rate-limit events on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency is selected, structured\n15\t    logging is configured on the Envoy/gateway enforcement layer instead of Authorino/Limitador;\n16\t    if this epic is dropped with the contingency, its scope folds into the contingency\n17\t    branch.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Configure structured logging for Kuadrant auth and rate-limit events on xKS\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDeliver the RHCL/OpenShift-team portion of the strategy's logging requirement: structured logging configuration for the Kuadrant components on xKS — Authorino authentication decisions and Limitador rate-limit enforcement events — formatted as structured JSON for aggregation in the CKS Grafana Loki infrastructure. Authorino and Limitador require no code changes for xKS (TokenRateLimitPolicy works on any Kubernetes); this is configuration work owned by the RHCL / OpenShift team per the strategy's affected-components and impacted-teams tables.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Configure Authorino to emit structured logs for authentication decisions (success/failure, identity, method, reason) in the field format the strategy's acceptance criteria require: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason if denied.\n44\t- Configure Limitador to emit structured logs for rate-limit enforcement decisions (including 429 responses with exceeded quota).\n45\t- Ensure both log streams are formatted for CKS Grafana Loki label-filter aggregation.\n46\t- Provide OIDC identity-source configuration guidance for Authorino on xKS (guidance deliverable, coordinated with the MaaS team's AuthPolicy configuration).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Authorino emits structured JSON authentication-decision logs containing timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision, and reason (if denied), measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters during authentication traffic.\n51\t- Limitador emits structured JSON rate-limit enforcement logs including exceeded-quota events, measured by querying Grafana Loki during rate-limited traffic.\n52\t- Both configurations are reproducible via the deployment mechanism selected for Kuadrant on xKS, measured by redeploying from configuration alone.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-10 [P1]: Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement (Kuadrant portion: Authorino auth decisions and Limitador rate-limit enforcement).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"be9b1e64-5629-435d-a6a3-fb02d4f9b51a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:43.416Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a499e8c9bc08d29a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
