{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-840dc384022e8c9d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E010\n3\ttitle: Add distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n29\tgate_failure_impact:\n30\t  action: rewrite\n31\t  fallback_approach: If the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency is selected for the\n32\t    auth/rate-limiting layer, the traced enforcement segments are rewritten to cover\n33\t    the Envoy ext_authz filter path instead of Authorino and Limitador; the MaaS-handled\n34\t    segments (gateway ingress, payload-processing, model backend) are unaffected.\n35\t---\n36\t# Add distributed tracing through the MaaS request path\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tImplement distributed tracing across the MaaS request path on xKS — gateway ingress through the enforcement layer (Authorino and Limitador, or the Envoy ext_authz filter, per the resolved deployment mechanism), payload-processing, to the model backend — using OpenTelemetry. This is the strategy's P2 observability tier. maas-api already integrates the OpenTelemetry SDK and exports traces via OTLP/gRPC to a collector (architecture context: maas-api/internal/tracing/provider.go), so the work extends an existing foundation to cover the full request path. The traced enforcement segments depend on which deployment mechanism the RHCL/Kuadrant deployment-mechanism investigation selects, so this epic is gated on that investigation's outcome and its scope adapts to the selected mechanism.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Propagate trace context through the full request path: gateway → enforcement layer (Authorino and Limitador on the Kuadrant paths, or the Envoy ext_authz filter on the contingency path, per the resolved deployment mechanism) → payload-processing (BBR ext_proc) → model backend.\n45\t- Emit spans for the MaaS-handled segments (maas-api request handling, payload-processing request transformations) via the existing OTel/OTLP export path.\n46\t- Configure trace collection compatible with the xKS observability infrastructure.\n47\t- Validate end-to-end trace continuity on a deployed MaaS instance on CKS, with the enforcement layer deployed per the resolved deployment mechanism (the mechanism-dependent deployment runs against the same validated instance; because that deployment is conditional, this ordering is expressed as the mechanism gate plus this scheduling note rather than a DAG edge from a main-plan epic to a conditional branch).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with tracing enabled and the enforcement layer in place per the resolved deployment mechanism, when an inference request is made, then a distributed trace exists covering gateway ingress, the selected mechanism's authentication and rate-limiting enforcement segments (Authorino authentication and Limitador rate limiting on the Kuadrant paths, or the Envoy ext_authz filter on the contingency path), payload-processing, and the model backend, measured by retrieving a complete trace (single trace ID across all segments) from the tracing backend.\n52\t- Tracing instrumentation does not observably degrade request latency, measured by load-test comparison before/after.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-13 [P2]: Distributed tracing functional: gateway → Authorino → Limitador → payload-processing → backend (per Staff Engineer Input).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"c2c11a98-4b03-452b-b55b-49f9f35187d5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:44.598Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-840dc384022e8c9d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
