{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-909760bf50fecb1e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E013\n3\ttitle: Implement configurable groupClaimPath in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD turns out to be frozen after deeper analysis,\n17\t    switch to documenting the required OIDC group claim format and pushing IdP configuration\n18\t    burden to customers.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Implement configurable groupClaimPath in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional plan (outcome A of the group-claim configurability investigation): the Tenant CRD is extensible post-3.4-GA, so a configurable `groupClaimPath` field is added (default `auth.identity.groups`) and passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation. This lets deployments map OIDC group claims with differing formats (Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) to subscription tiers without code changes per identity provider.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Add the `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD schema (default: `auth.identity.groups`).\n44\t- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation (maas-controller/pkg/controller/maas/maassubscription_controller.go), so tier-mapping predicates read groups from the configured OIDC claim path.\n45\t- Expose `groupClaimPath` as a Helm chart value so the deployment configuration drives it per deployment.\n46\t- Keep the change additive/configuration-driven: RHOAI MaaS GA behavior with the default value is unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n47\t- Validate the claim-path tier mapping end-to-end on the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS (the CKS validation deployment). The tier-enforcement measurement presumes the authentication and rate-limiting enforcement layer is deployed on that instance per the resolved deployment mechanism — deployed by the selected deployment-mechanism branch against the same validated instance. Because that deployment is itself conditional, this presupposition is expressed as the CKS-deployment dependency plus this scheduling note rather than a DAG edge between conditional branches.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement on the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS, with the enforcement layer in place per the resolved deployment mechanism.\n52\t- Given a deployment using the default claim path, when group-based tier mapping is exercised, then behavior is identical to the current (RHOAI) implementation, measured by existing tier-mapping tests passing unchanged.\n53\t- The field is configurable per deployment via the Helm chart, measured by rendering with a non-default claim path producing the corresponding Tenant configuration.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n58\t- HLR-9 [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"046a00be-7790-407f-a87f-10dfe6be6875","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:56.595Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-909760bf50fecb1e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 2"}
