{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-869bbe115625fedf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E013\n3\ttitle: Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD is later opened for extension, replace this\n17\t    documentation-only fallback with the configurable groupClaimPath implementation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS on xKS\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional plan (outcome B of the group-claim configurability investigation): the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA, so configurable claim-path mapping cannot be shipped. Instead, the required OIDC group claim format is documented and identity-provider configuration burden is pushed to customers: customers must configure their IdP (or token transformation) to emit groups in the claim format MaaS expects (`auth.identity.groups`).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Document the required OIDC group claim format for MaaS tier/subscription mapping on xKS, including concrete IdP configuration guidance for common providers (e.g., Entra ID, Cognito, Keycloak) to emit or map groups into the required claim.\n43\t- Document this as a known limitation of the xKS Dev Preview versus configurable claim-path mapping.\n44\t- Verify the documented guidance against at least one real identity provider configuration on the CKS validation deployment, so tier mapping works end-to-end with a correctly configured IdP.\n45\t- The tier-mapping verification presumes the authentication and rate-limiting enforcement layer is deployed on the CKS validation deployment per the resolved deployment mechanism — deployed by the selected deployment-mechanism branch against the same validated instance. Because that deployment is itself conditional, this presupposition is expressed as the CKS-deployment dependency plus this scheduling note rather than a DAG edge between conditional branches.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A document exists specifying the required OIDC group claim format and per-provider configuration steps, measured by publication and review.\n50\t- Given an OIDC deployment whose IdP is configured per the document, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the user is mapped to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement on the CKS validation deployment, with the enforcement layer in place per the resolved deployment mechanism.\n51\t- The limitation (no configurable claim path in the Dev Preview) is recorded in the known-limitations document, measured by its inclusion.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-6 [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (fallback: documented required claim format; per-strategy fallback if the Tenant CRD is frozen).\n56\t- HLR-9 [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (via documented claim format).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38984b32dc22156","agent_id":"a883bf37defa5d7fe","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"3737afd8-f89c-47aa-b38d-26a5a19f779f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:13:57.695Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-to