{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9098e48879a85b89","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8003\n3\tscore: 11\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'Missing DAG edge E008 -> E006: E006 (maas-api structured logging)\n10\t    has dependencies: [] yet its acceptance criteria are measured by querying Grafana\n11\t    Loki against a deployed MaaS instance — the same validated-on-deployed-instance\n12\t    rule the decomposition itself applied to add E008 dependencies to E007 (revision\n13\t    note 3) and E010 (revision note 6). Add the E008 -> E006 edge to E006 frontmatter\n14\t    dependencies and the summary DAG diagram (E006 may still start in parallel with\n15\t    E005; only its Loki-queried validation ACs presuppose the E008 deployment).'\n16\t- severity: minor\n17\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n18\t  description: 'E005 ai_signals.open_questions: 0 is arguable: the strategy assumption\n19\t    table marks maas-api instrumentation feasibility without 3.4 GA code changes as\n20\t    Needs validation and the epic scope branches on it (direct delivery vs post-3.4\n21\t    patch); -1 is at least as accurate.'\n22\t- severity: minor\n23\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n24\t  description: 'E006 ai_signals.open_questions: 1 and external_dependency: 0 are arguable:\n25\t    the epic ACs are measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki, whose accessibility for\n26\t    MaaS is a strategy assumption marked Needs validation and owned by no epic.'\n27\t- severity: minor\n28\t  criterion: Acceptance Criteria Quality\n29\t  description: BRANCH-A-E012 AC measured by a written statement from the RHCL/OpenShift\n30\t    team makes an external team deliverable the AC measurement; keep the documentation-of-terms\n31\t    AC and move the written-statement expectation to Risks/Notes.\n32\t- severity: minor\n33\