{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9016614b972238af","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: Add structured logging to maas-api for xKS observability\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Add structured logging to maas-api for xKS observability\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd structured (JSON) logging to maas-api covering authentication-related events (API key validation outcomes) and subscription selection decisions, formatted for aggregation in the CKS Grafana Loki infrastructure. This is the maas-api portion of the strategy's P1 logging requirement; Kuadrant-side (Authorino/Limitador) log configuration is separately owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Emit structured JSON log entries for:\n38\t  - API key validation events (success/failure, with reason).\n39\t  - Subscription selection decisions (which tier/subscription was selected for a request).\n40\t- Include the fields the strategy's acceptance criteria require: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason if denied.\n41\t- Format logs with labels/structure suitable for CKS Grafana Loki label-filter queries.\n42\t- Reuse the existing zap structured logging already present in the maas-api codebase.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n47\t- Given a request that triggers subscription selection, when the selection is made, then the decision is logged with the selected subscription/tier, measured by querying Grafana Loki.\n48\t- Log entries are valid structured JSON parseable by the Loki aggregation pipeline, measured by a log pipeline dry-run against sample output.\n49\t- Logging overhead does not observably degrade request latency, measured by load-test comparison before/after.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-10 [P1]: Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (maas-api portion: authentication/API key events and subscription selection).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-949830f290ee01a8","agent_id":"ab0f9faf32e1f9a83","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"9ff1cba0-fc40-485a-b60d-cf5893c5e0ae","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:20:16.639Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9016614b972238af","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final revise RHAISTRAT-8003"}
