{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9d7862b52ab468a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: Package MaaS components as Helm charts for xKS deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Package MaaS components as Helm charts for xKS deployment\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tPackage the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) as Helm charts for xKS deployment, replacing OLM-based operator installation (explicitly out of scope for xKS per the RFE — Helm only). This is the packaging foundation for deploying and validating MaaS on CKS and AKS.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Create Helm charts for the MaaS components with configurable values for:\n38\t  - Gateway class name (not `openshift-default`; Istio for CKS, with envoy-gateway / azure-application-gateway as future options).\n39\t  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience).\n40\t  - TLS certificate source (cert-manager instead of OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates).\n41\t  - PostgreSQL connection (shared with other RHAII components or dedicated — open question resolved as a chart value, not a structural decision).\n42\t- Remove OpenShift-specific installation assumptions (OLM, OpenShift namespaces/service-CA) from the chart rendering path.\n43\t- Support the HTTPRoute-based routing documented in the architecture context (GatewayClass-agnostic HTTPRoutes) so the chart binds to the target platform's GatewayClass.\n44\t- Ensure the chart is consumable by the RHAII xKS deployment/installation strategy (xKS Platform collaboration).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- `helm install` of the chart on a Kubernetes cluster with a non-OpenShift GatewayClass renders all MaaS workloads (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing), measured by successful rendering and pod readiness in a test cluster.\n49\t- Gateway class name, OIDC issuer settings, TLS certificate source, and PostgreSQL connection are all configurable via chart values, measured by rendering with non-default values producing the corresponding resources.\n50\t- No OLM or OpenShift-specific resource types are required by the chart, measured by a dry-run render against plain Kubernetes CRDs.\n51\t- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager (not OpenShift service-CA), measured by successful certificate provisioning on a cluster with cert-manager installed.\n52\t- The RHAII xKS installation chart (owned by the xKS Platform team) consumes the MaaS chart as a named subchart or dependency, measured by a successful `helm template` render of the umbrella chart that produces the MaaS workloads with the MaaS chart's values (gateway class, OIDC issuer settings, TLS source, PostgreSQL connection) propagated from the umbrella chart's values.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-1 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (packaging enabler).\n57\t- HLR-2 [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (packaging enabler).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a408e5be687f31bc","agent_id":"a2ebc6856d3219725","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"c0fbc06a-d176-41f0-b55d-1f8dad64e547","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:25:41.241Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9d7862b52ab468a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 3"}
