{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89965666455460f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: Add structured logging to maas-api for xKS observability\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Add structured logging to maas-api for xKS observability\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAdd structured (JSON) logging to maas-api covering authentication-related events (API key validation outcomes) and subscription selection decisions, formatted for aggregation in the CKS Grafana Loki infrastructure. This is the maas-api portion of the strategy's P1 logging requirement; Kuadrant-side (Authorino/Limitador) log configuration is separately owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Emit structured JSON log entries for:\n39\t  - API key validation events (success/failure, with reason).\n40\t  - Subscription selection decisions (which tier/subscription was selected for a request).\n41\t- Include the fields the strategy's acceptance criteria require: timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason if denied.\n42\t- Format logs with labels/structure suitable for CKS Grafana Loki label-filter queries.\n43\t- Reuse the existing zap structured logging already present in the maas-api codebase.\n44\t- Validate the strategy assumption that CKS Grafana Loki log aggregation is accessible for MaaS logs (marked \"Needs validation\"; owner per the strategy's open-questions table: xKS Platform / CoreWeave) — confirm accessibility or escalate the gap, mirroring the Prometheus scrape-target confirmation on the metrics integration side.\n45\t- The Loki-queried acceptance criteria below are exercised against the MaaS instance deployed and validated on CKS — the deployed-instance prerequisite that orders this epic after the CKS/AKS deployment validation work (the logging code changes themselves are independent of it).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n50\t- Given a request that triggers subscription selection, when the selection is made, then the decision is logged with the selected subscription/tier, measured by querying Grafana Loki.\n51\t- Log entries are valid structured JSON parseable by the Loki aggregation pipeline, measured by a log pipeline dry-run against sample output.\n52\t- CKS Grafana Loki log-aggregation accessibility for MaaS logs is confirmed and documented (or the gap escalated to the xKS Platform / CoreWeave owners), measured by Loki label-filter queries returning maas-api log entries from the deployed instance.\n53\t- Logging overhead does not observably degrade request latency, measured by load-test comparison before/after.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-10 [P1]: Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (maas-api portion: authentication/API key events and subscription selection).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a408e5be687f31bc","agent_id":"a2ebc6856d3219725","session_id":"50e38564-4e5e-45db-b1e4-649369677e1e","uuid":"8d8a1b08-78fb-47fa-967b-4d694ef1039f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:25:45.892Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89965666455460f0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 round 3"}
